# Example enclave config (placeholder hosts and values). Both files of a
# config dir are measured into PCR2, so they hold no secrets: the wallet key,
# WS RPC URL and Postgres connection string are delivered at runtime (not yet
# implemented). `environment` is passed to key-gen verbatim by nit, one
# KEY=VALUE per line, so it cannot carry comments or blank lines.
#
# The parent side is oprf-enclave-host, which reads this same file:
# outbound <host> <port> <vsock-port>: <host> resolves to its own 127.0.0.x
# inside the enclave; connections go to the parent (CID 3) on <vsock-port>,
# where the host proxy dials <host>:<port>.
# inbound <tcp-port> <vsock-port>: the host listens on TCP <tcp-port> and
# connects to the enclave on <vsock-port>, which reaches 127.0.0.1:<tcp-port>.
outbound db.example.internal 5432 8001
outbound rpc.example.com 443 8002
outbound ws.rpc.example.com 443 8003
inbound 4321 4321
